@startuml server_profile_validation
!theme cyborg
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam backgroundColor #0b1018
skinparam defaultFontColor #e6edf7
skinparam ArrowColor #a9b8ca
skinparam activity {
 BackgroundColor #111826
 BorderColor #a9b8ca
 DiamondBackgroundColor #273241
}
skinparam swimlane {
 BorderColor #61738a
 TitleFontColor #e6edf7
}
title Server profile: which check runs where, when, and what a failure does

|Developer PC: server profile tool|
start
:1. Input validation (check)
TOML format 1, known keys, canonical HTTPS URL
certificate rules 1 to 5, rule 4 on the PC date;
if (file and certificate valid?) then (no)
 :Exit 1, key and rule named; <<#3b2a1a>>
 detach
endif
:2. Image construction (build)
fields, CRC-32, size within the partition
taken from the build devicetree;
if (image fits the partition?) then (no)
 :Rejected before writing; <<#3b2a1a>>
 detach
endif
:Flash command writes only the image,
esptool verifies the written data;

|Device boot, once|
:3. L1_STORAGE structural checks
erased, magic, version, lengths, CRC-32;
if (image structurally valid?) then (no)
 :Missing or invalid image:
 secure transport unavailable,
 Wi-Fi setup and offline listening continue; <<#3b2a1a>>
 detach
endif
:4. L2_COMMUNICATION keep-alive check
server keep-alive must exceed 5 s;
if (keep-alive above 5 s?) then (no)
 :Invalid configuration, rule logged:
 secure transport unavailable,
 Wi-Fi setup and offline listening continue; <<#3b2a1a>>
 detach
endif
:5. L1_WIFI endpoint and certificate checks
usable URL, exactly one parsable certificate,
Subject Alternative Name matching the host type;
if (configuration valid?) then (no)
 :Invalid configuration, rule logged:
 secure transport unavailable,
 Wi-Fi setup and offline listening continue; <<#3b2a1a>>
 detach
endif

|Each secure connection setup|
:SNTP exchange inside the setup;
:6. L2_COMMUNICATION pre-handshake validity
certificate validity against the prepared UTC time;
if (valid at that time?) then (no)
 :No ClientHello sent,
 SERVER_CONNECTION_FAILURE path, later retry; <<#3b2a1a>>
 detach
endif
:7. L1_WIFI handshake verification (mbedTLS)
TLS 1.3, verification required, only this
certificate trusted; Key Usage and Extended
Key Usage (rule 5); peer dates again;
if (handshake verified?) then (no)
 :Connection fails,
 failure handled by the TLS design; <<#3b2a1a>>
 detach
endif
:Verified connection retained at most for the
server keep-alive minus 5 s or the clock-anchor limit;
stop

legend bottom left
 COMMUNICATION checks the keep-alive before it hands URL and certificate to L1_WIFI.
 Device-side rule 2 (self-issued, self-signature) needs implementation evidence: the device configures the certificate as the only
 trust anchor, but no device test shows that verification rejects a directly trusted certificate that is not self-issued.
 The CRC-32 detects corruption, not tampering; the image has no signature.
endlegend
@enduml
